meric type T."},{"label":"Return value","children":[{"label":"/* non-specialized */","note":"T()"},{"label":"bool","note":"false"},{"label":"char","note":"CHAR_MIN"},{"label":"signed char","note":"SCHAR_MIN"},{"label":"unsigned char","note":"0"},{"label":"wchar_t","note":"WCHAR_MIN"},{"label":"char8_t (since C++20)","note":"0"},{"label":"+13 more"}]},{"label":"Example","note":"Demonstrates the use with typedef types, and the difference in the sign of the result between integer and floating-point types:"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"lowest","note":"returns the lowest finite value of the given type, i.e. the most negative value for signed types, 0 for unsigned types"},{"label":"denorm_min","note":"returns the smallest positive subnormal value of the given floating-point type"},{"label":"max","note":"returns the largest finite value of the given type"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":423,"codeBlockCount":2}
